WEBVTT

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:08.480
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Wednesday, 11 February. Can you all hear me, or am I doing the Teams mime again?</v>

00:00:09.449 --> 00:00:15.050
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, got you. Sorry, just sat down. The traffic on the ring road was absolutely solid.</v>

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:24.550
<v Marcus Hale>Lovely, isn't it? I'm meant to be going walking at the weekend, but looking at this weather, my weekend plans might just be the sofa.</v>

00:00:26.899 --> 00:00:31.100
<v Tomasz Nowak>Probably get further on the sofa than I did in the car.</v>

00:00:32.729 --> 00:00:40.079
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. There's a birthday cake in the office, by the way. Already there, before anyone adds cake procurement to the list.</v>

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.189
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Finally, a job with decent materials availability.</v>

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:49.619
<v Sarah Okafor>Behave. Fi, anything closed out before we get into the live stuff?</v>

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:56.039
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, signed off the inspection on the fire panel on Tuesday. That's finished.</v>

00:00:56.409 --> 00:01:02.359
<v Fiona Doyle>And signed off the inspection on the stretch wrapper on Tuesday as well. Both closed, not carry-overs.</v>

00:01:03.219 --> 00:01:08.819
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers. I signed off the inspection on the line 3 chiller on Tuesday too. That's done.</v>

00:01:09.719 --> 00:01:16.019
<v Priya Raman>On the stretch wrapper, I noticed it was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down.</v>

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:20.370
<v Hannah Price>Sorry, are you saying there's something outstanding against that inspection?</v>

00:01:22.629 --> 00:01:26.829
<v Priya Raman>No, no—just an observation. Settled down, nothing new to action from me.</v>

00:01:27.859 --> 00:01:35.209
<v Fiona Doyle>Same sort of thing, I heard a slight rattle from the IM3. Nothing to action yet, just mentioning what I heard.</v>

00:01:37.159 --> 00:01:41.709
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Understood. Not turning every noise in the building into a work order, then.</v>

00:01:42.879 --> 00:01:51.629
<v Fiona Doyle>And we were going to replace the belt on the line 2 interlock, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it for today.</v>

00:01:53.519 --> 00:01:58.420
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine. Closed items, observations and that deferred belt all stay off today's action list.</v>

00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:07.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Hannah, can you inspect the GT1 fuel valve for leaks by Monday? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:13.800
<v Hannah Price>Monday is the deadline, but first in the queue because of the production hold, yeah?</v>

00:02:15.889 --> 00:02:20.789
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Monday isn't an invitation to leave it sitting there. It needs doing first.</v>

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:27.960
<v Hannah Price>Understood. I'll inspect the GT1 fuel valve for leaks, first in my queue, by Monday.</v>

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:36.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Priya, can you run a function test on the line 1 TCU by Wednesday? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:39.189
<v Priya Raman>By Wednesday—we're talking today, aren't we?</v>

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:44.780
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, today. That's the Wednesday deadline, and drop everything for it.</v>

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:53.159
<v Priya Raman>Right, accepted. I'll run a function test on the line 1 TCU by Wednesday. That's my immediate priority.</v>

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:57.599
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, clear. That's not one buried halfway down the list.</v>

00:02:59.229 --> 00:03:07.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Priya, can I also give you scheduling downtime for the palletizer with production, at half two? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:17.930
<v Priya Raman>Um, no, I can't take that as well. Not with the function test you've just put first. That'd be me saying yes and then dropping it.</v>

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:26.490
<v Fiona Doyle>Fair enough. Sarah Okafor, can that come back to you, then—schedule downtime for the palletizer with production at half two?</v>

00:03:28.419 --> 00:03:38.219
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, I'll take it instead of Priya. I'll schedule downtime for the palletizer with production at half two. Not an emergency but don't let it slip—that still stands.</v>

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:46.719
<v Fiona Doyle>And half two is when you're doing the scheduling, not us announcing that the machine stops at half two?</v>

00:03:48.330 --> 00:03:52.530
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct. Scheduling with production. We haven't agreed the actual downtime slot here.</v>

00:03:54.520 --> 00:04:00.469
<v Fiona Doyle>While we're on half two, I'll grease and check the bearings on the GT2 at half two.</v>

00:04:02.969 --> 00:04:06.819
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, talked over you. Bearings at half two, did you say?</v>

00:04:08.930 --> 00:04:16.629
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah. I'll grease and check them at half two. Not an emergency but don't let it slip is how I'm treating that.</v>

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:21.589
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fi. The GT2 bearings are yours, then.</v>

00:04:23.339 --> 00:04:27.189
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Planner with a grease gun. The spreadsheet's going to get fingerprints.</v>

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.790
<v Fiona Doyle>It'll survive. Might improve some of the numbers.</v>

00:04:31.089 --> 00:04:37.389
<v Sarah Okafor>Marcus, can you swap the filter on the AC1 today? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:39.110 --> 00:04:42.259
<v Marcus Hale>Yep, I'll swap the filter on the AC1 today.</v>

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:46.120
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Was that another half-two one, or—sorry, the audio clipped.</v>

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:53.360
<v Sarah Okafor>No, today for that one, no particular clock time. Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:57.199
<v Marcus Hale>Got it. Today, and it stays on my list.</v>

00:04:57.959 --> 00:05:08.110
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz, can you go to Tollgate to pick up the replacement parts for the line 3 barrel by the end of the week? That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:05:08.829 --> 00:05:17.930
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, so get straight onto that, with the collection completed by the end of the week? Not wait until the end of the week to start.</v>

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:24.649
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Safety critical, straight away. By the end of the week is the deadline.</v>

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:34.139
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, I'll go to Tollgate to pick up the replacement parts for the line 3 barrel. Straight onto it, completed by the end of the week.</v>

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:40.959
<v Hannah Price>That's separate from the guarding item, isn't it? Don't want those getting bundled together.</v>

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:50.069
<v Sarah Okafor>It is. I'll check the guarding on the Injection Moulding Line 3 by the end of the week. It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:58.850
<v Fiona Doyle>Got that, Saz. Guarding is yours, by the end of the week, and not the same urgency as the parts.</v>

00:06:00.439 --> 00:06:02.889
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, exactly. Two separate things, different priorities.</v>

00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:14.649
<v Priya Raman>Before we get too far, I still can't get to the water booster until production gives us a window. That's a blocker, not me volunteering for anything else.</v>

00:06:16.279 --> 00:06:22.579
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. I'll replace the seals on the Water Booster Pump after lunch. That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:30.379
<v Priya Raman>Just to be clear, though, we haven't got that production window confirmed. After lunch isn't confirmed access.</v>

00:06:31.189 --> 00:06:44.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Agreed, I'm not saying the blocker's cleared. I'll own the seal replacement, with after lunch as the planned timing, subject to that access. Safety critical, straight away once we can get in—not a casual job to leave sitting.</v>

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:54.250
<v Fiona Doyle>So Sarah owns the Water Booster Pump seals, after lunch, and the access blocker stays visible. Not marked ready when it isn't.</v>

00:06:55.939 --> 00:06:57.689
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, that's the honest version.</v>

00:06:59.149 --> 00:07:05.100
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Was there a controls item for next week as well? I lost the thread when Teams froze.</v>

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:10.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah. I'll recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 water valve next week.</v>

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:17.459
<v Fiona Doyle>Sarah Okafor against the GT2 water valve sensor recalibration, next week. That's you taking it, yes?</v>

00:07:19.579 --> 00:07:21.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, I'll do that next week.</v>

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:28.959
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Right, distinct from the bearings. Same machine label floating about, different bit of kit.</v>

00:07:30.389 --> 00:07:32.490
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. No bundling those together either.</v>

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:37.220
<v Marcus Hale>Lovely. And the weather's somehow got worse while we've been talking.</v>

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:40.430
<v Tomasz Nowak>Sofa weekend looking stronger by the minute.</v>

00:07:42.199 --> 00:07:46.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, cheers everyone. That's the stand-up. Cake's in the office, rain's everywhere else.</v>
